A precision approach path indicator (PAPI) is a system of four lights on the side of an airport runway threshold that provides visual descent guidance information during final approach. It is generally located on the left side of the runway approximately 300 metres (980 ft) beyond the landing threshold of the runway.
A typical engineering design specification for each of the four PAPI light unit is shown below:
Optical construction:
Two lamps for redundancy;
Anodized aluminium reflectors;
Red color filter;
One or two lenses;
Lamps and reflectors replaceable without recalibration.
Each light unit consists of one or more light sources, red filters and lenses. A color filter may not be necessary with colored LED lights. Each light unit emits a high-intensity beam. The lower segment of the beam is red, and the upper part is white. The transition between the two colours must take place over an angle not greater than three minutes of arc.
